  "body": "**Stacked on #551** (EDM machine kinds). Its commits show here until #551 merges; this PR adds one commit on top.\n\n## What changed\n\n`edm.conditions[]` in the `.mch` `edm` section (#531, part of #290, design D4):\n- Each condition is `{ id, name, gap, wire_diameter | undersize, role: rough|skim|finish, notes }`. It holds only the geometry a toolpath needs. Power and flushing stay the control's, selected by `id`.\n- `id` is the control's own selector, required and unique; a numeric id reads as its word. Lengths scale with the file's unit. Gap and undersize may be 0; a wire diameter must be positive.\n- A garbled entry refuses the file, naming its id, and `is_sane` restates the law for project files.\n- `Edm::condition(machine, id, need)` is the door the first EDM op (#532) calls at command creation. A missing condition, or an unstated field the op needs (gap, wire diameter, undersize), is refused by name before any generator runs.\n- No conditions ship. Tests use an explicitly synthetic table.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `edm_conditions`, 6/6:\n  - a stated table reads, and the template states none;\n  - an inch file's gap reads in mm;\n  - the lookup refuses a missing condition or field by name;\n  - eight garbled tables each refuse the file;\n  - a hand-edited project machine with duplicate ids or a NaN gap is not sane;\n  - the table rides the project file.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick`, escalated to batch: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion and app are green, and clippy `-D warnings` is clean on all 8 crates. ui: only the five known reds that are also red on main.\n- Named: `edm_machine` 7, `machine` 32, `machine_library` 11, and `camcraft-post` all pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- An EDM op using the door; that is #532.\n- A real control's condition numbers; the data is the user's.\n\nChangelog: EDM machine files can state the generator conditions (spark gap, wire diameter, undersize) an EDM operation selects by id (#531)\n\nFixes #531\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
